# Closed-class words that never stand as a counted noun right after an hour:
# pronouns, adverbs and verb particles ("a las 8 te llamo").  Each word's class
# is quoted from its Wiktionary entry (https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/<word>); the
# fetched pages are kept with the audit.  Markup is removed from the quotes.
# em: Pronoun. "me (direct or indirect object)"
# et: Pronoun. "you, thee (singular, direct or indirect object)"
# el: Pronoun. "him (direct object)"
# la: Pronoun. "her (direct object)"
# li: Pronoun. "him, her, it (indirect object, singular all genders)"
# ens: Pronoun. "us (direct or indirect object)"
# us: Pronoun. "you (plural, direct or indirect object)"
# hi: Pronoun. "represents a place associated with the action described by the verb, unless the place would be introduced b..."
em
et
el
la
li
ens
us
hi
